    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The past agrees with the subject",
     "texto": [
      "As in English, the past does not change according to the person, but it agrees in **gender and number with the subject**. With я and ты, the form depends on the gender of the speaker or of the person being addressed.",
      "With many verbs, **-ть** is removed and **-л** (masculine singular), **-ла** (feminine singular), **-ло** (neuter singular) or **-ли** (plural) is added.",
      "работать → **работал** (masculine subject), **работала** (feminine), **работало** (neuter), **работали** (plural).",
      "Some verbs are irregular: идти forms **шёл, шла, шло, шли**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
